{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"gibbs-comparison","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:af309f3a8460be4f12868d9deae92e9f84ec7fddc91b81a77167a172951f75ea/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989","passage_ref":"sha256:2b095aacecc1f5d7007325207b199a16856277bccf9cd83f2e5f52f0d81b6ef8/papers/long.md/sha256:af309f3a8460be4f12868d9deae92e9f84ec7fddc91b81a77167a172951f75ea/papers/long.json/passages/gibbs-comparison","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","span":{"end_byte":221996,"end_line":4888,"start_byte":220083,"start_line":4847},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&ref=sha256%3A05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Ordinary derivation in this authored edition, not an attribution of the whole synthesis to a cited external paper. The log-sum and entropy identities give the deterministic bounds; Gaussian concentration uses Lipschitz constant sqrt((n-1)/(2n^2)); counting configurations gives the conditional tail. Exact Gibbs sampling is a distributional premise, not an efficient sampling algorithm. The Born law and QAOA angle construction are distinct. No Lean or Comparator coverage and no complete formal dependency audit are asserted.","citation_ids":["authored_gibbs_comparison","scalar-r2-26-cite-parisi-formula"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"Finite Gibbs values and exact Gibbs samples","locator":"papers/qaoa-sk/long/reasoning-record.md §11.1.2, passage:gibbs-comparison; content-addressed source edition, not an external-paper attribution.","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For the pure zero-field SK Hamiltonian and beta>0, let L_n=max_sigma H_n(sigma)/n, F_n,beta=(n beta)^(-1)log sum_sigma exp(beta H_n(sigma)), and U_n,beta be the exact Gibbs mean energy per spin. For each instance, 0<=F_n,beta-L_n<=log(2)/beta and 0<=L_n-U_n,beta<=log(2)/beta. For n>=2 and s>0, P_J(|L_n-E L_n|>s)<=2 exp(-n^2 s^2/(n-1)). For an exact Gibbs draw Sigma, P(H_n(Sigma)/n<=L_n-s | J)<=min(1,exp(n(log(2)-beta s))). Since E L_n tends to P_*, both value expectations tend to P_* along every joint n→infinity,beta→infinity; an exact Gibbs draw tends to P_* in the joint disorder-and-sampling probability.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"sup